dictadesk (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Run exclusively in the system tray, with standalone Preferences.
  * Bind dictation to the original window and editable field across focus changes.
  * Restore selections where supported and retain text when insertion is unsafe.
  * Add a compact tray reference and preserve configurable dictation shortcuts.
  * Keep settings and reference windows independent and support Escape dismissal.
  * Clarify model setup and allow microphone tests with selected unsaved options.
  * Remove blocking transcript recovery; copy failed insertions to the clipboard.
  * Recover recording state after cancellation, empty results and processing errors.
  * Add private metadata diagnostics and bounded speech-worker communication.
  * Keep panel icon sizing and artwork consistent across state changes.
  * Separate shared settings from dictation and optional feature preferences.
  * Improve recognition feedback and tolerate bounded transcription variants.

 -- Erick Woods <woodpile72@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 15:57:05 +0000

